        {
          "question": "q-325108",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}={x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nUsing the implicit Euler method with step size $\u0394x=0.25,$ the new value ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ is obtained by solving the equation $g({y}_{\\text{new}})=0$ at each step.\nWhich of the following is the **general form** of $g({y}_{\\text{new}})$ in terms of the new values ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}},$ and the current value $y?$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067403/state.json",
          "file_sha256": "7f679b8b1fefcf14f792843c723eafae81d78bf482d2259f74cda2d9f2f61b34"
        }
      ],
